<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 falls 3.6 pct, M2 down 2.2 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 falls 3.6 pct, M2 down 2.2 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply fell to 579.9 billion levs on April 25 from 601.6 billion levs a week earlier and M2 edged down to 2,976.6 billion levs from 3044.2 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>&quot;M1 decreased due to a fall of call deposits, which is usual at the end of each month, as companies and individuals withdraw money for pending payments, to repay credits or buy government securities,&quot; a central bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Total broad money fell 2.45 percent to 3,138.4 billion levs in the week to April 25.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at un exchange rate of 1,467.8 levs per dollar on April 25 against 1,500.3 on April 18 and 1,590.8 on March 28.</p>
